                "submission_id": "submission:correctness-review:1:899485a2",
                "summary": "src/teach/fit.ts:37-46: when the matcher answers unknown/too_far because the CLOSEST concept is another one (ranked[0].conceptId !== conceptId, beyond that concept's limit) and the concept's own comparable examples are within the concept's own limit, exampleFit falls through to {kind:'differs'}. That contradicts the 'differs' contract (fit.ts:20-21 and AC1: 'beyond the concept's limit') and the comment at fit.ts:37 ('or closest to another one'), and the caregiver is told 'deutlich anders als die bisherigen Beispiele ... War es dieselbe Gebärde?' (caregiver.ts fitLine) instead of the look-alike warning. Reproduced with synthetic blends (dist build, matcher unchanged): ranked [oth 0.774, own 0.776], own limit 1.155, oth limit 0.750 -> exampleFit = differs; second case [oth 0.817, own 0.876], own limit 0.882 -> differs. Fix (local, no threshold change): after the ambiguous check, if result.reason==='too_far' and ranked[0] exists with conceptId!==conceptId, return {kind:'resembles', otherId: ranked[0].conceptId} (or only when the own distance is within limitKey(conceptId, sequence)'s calibrated limit); add a synthetic test in test/teach.test.mjs for that case. Otherwise verified: replaySteps inverts writeHand layout (offset side*43, shape 40 values /SHAPE_WEIGHT, wrist at 40/41, presence at 42; mirroring negates wrist x and joint dx consistently; presence after resample is exactly 1 inside the hand's span, fractional boundary steps are dropped); no file under src/recognition changed; fit is keyed on result identity so Verwerfen/Behalten/new recording cannot show a stale line; replay timer stops via teaching(open) + state.replay identity, replayCanvas reset each teachView build, busy clears replay.",
